    "title": "East Grand Rapids' Gaslight Village to host inaugural fine art fair - NewsBreak",
    "text": "By Zach Avery ,\n12 hours ago\nEAST GRAND RAPIDS, Mich. (WOOD) — Beginning Friday, visitors to the Gaslight Village shopping district in East Grand Rapids can attend the inaugural East Grand Rapids Fine Art Fair , a new event from The Guild of Artists & Artisans .\n“We’re thrilled to introduce a new fine art fair that reflects both the sophistication and warmth of the East Grand Rapids community,” Karen Delhey, executive director of The Guild of Artists & Artisans, said in a statement.\nList: Pride Month events in West Michigan 2026 Over 100 artists will participate in this year’s art fair, and each vendor has been selected after a competitive jury process.\n“We received numerous requests from both artists and community members to bring this event to the area and are delighted to see it come to fruition,” Delhey said in a statement.\nPera Pizzeria in Gaslight Village. Participating artists in the East Grand Rapids Fine Art Fair. (Courtesy) Participating artists in the East Grand Rapids Fine Art Fair. (Courtesy) As visitors stroll through Gaslight Village and shop with each art vendor, guests can enjoy live music and all-ages, interactive activities.\nThe East Grand Rapids Fine Art Fair is free to attend and will take place from Friday to Sunday. It will be open 3 p.m. to 7 p.m. on Friday, 10 a.m. to 7 p.m. on Saturday and 10 a.m. to 4 p.m. on Sunday.\nThe East Grand Rapids Fine Art Fair. (Courtesy) Participating artists in the East Grand Rapids Fine Art Fair. (Courtesy) Participating artists in the East Grand Rapids Fine Art Fair. (Courtesy) For more, visit The Guild of Artists & Artisans’ website .\nCopyright 2026 Nexstar Media, Inc. All rights reserved. This material may not be published, broadcast, rewritten, or redistributed. For the latest news, weather, sports, and streaming video, head to WOODTV.com.",
    "summary": "“We’re thrilled to introduce a new fine art fair that reflects both the sophistication and warmth of the East Grand Rapids community,” Karen Delhey, executive director of The Guild of Artists & Artisans, said in a statement. List: Pride Month events in West Michigan 2026 Over 100 artists will participate in this year’s art fair, and each vendor has been selected after a competitive jury process. “We received numerous requests from both artists and community members to bring this event to the area and are delighted to see it come to fruition,” Delhey said in a statement.",
